From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:52:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DLSS frame generation keeps the UI in place: a HUD-less input

The game draws its UI (the crosshair, the HUD, menus) over the path traced image after RTX injection,
and DLSS Frame Generation was given only the finished back buffer with motion vectors and depth. It
moved every pixel with the scene's motion, the UI's too: a crosshair over a turning view smeared or
doubled in each generated frame. NGX takes an optional HUD-less colour, the frame before its UI, and
keeps the pixels where the back buffer differs from it (the UI) in place.

- The D3D9 swapchain keeps, while the frame generation presenter runs, a copy of its back buffer (its
  create info and its sampled view) and hands it to DxvkDLFG's DlfgHudlessHandoff.
- Injection blits the final output into that copy right after it blits it into the game's target, when
  frame generation is on and the copy has the target's size, format and one sample, and marks the frame.
- The DLFG presenter has a HUD-less image beside each back buffer; the swapchain's present blits the
  copy into it with the same blitter call as the back buffer's (same rects, gamma ramp, view), so a pixel
  no UI was drawn over comes out identical.
- The present thread passes the slot's HUD-less image to NGX_VK_EVALUATE_DLSSG (pHudless) only for a
  frame the render thread marked; a new copy (another back buffer size or format) forgets every mark.
  Its barriers mirror the back buffer's (present layout to shader read and back).

rtx_dlfg_hudless.h is self-contained; tests/rtx/unit/test_dlfg_hudless.cpp covers the handoff (frames,
copies replaced and dropped, the render and presenter threads). FSR frame generation already gets the
final output as its HUD-less colour. Frame generation off: nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
